                                                "sense_id": "9787cced-97cc-3065-9d7b-213eb85c5b0b",
                                                "text": "Dieselisation saw the withdrawal of Shay engines on the Western Maryland, but No. 6 was rescued from an inglorious demise on the scrap heap, and now rests in the Baltimore & Ohio Railroad's transport museum in Baltimore, which contains many other interesting railway exhibits."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a77c5e72-88e6-469e-9d76-34a183f4859a",
                                                "sense_id": "9787cced-97cc-3065-9d7b-213eb85c5b0b",
                                                "text": "The large double-deck Brush electric cars which replaced steam in 1929 and were the largest passenger-carrying road vehicles in the country, will follow the fixed assets to the scrap heap."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
